#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example shows a Braking Distance Test for a full-size pickup truck with ABS.
#
#In this test procedure, the vehicle is traveling at 102 km/h at the start of the simulation and coasts down to 100  km/h.  Using Events, the car is repositioned to the start of the road (0 m) and simultaneously begins to brake. Review the plot of Station vs. Time to measure the vehicle's braking distance.
#
#NOTE: Master cylinder brake pressure is used as the driver brake control.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

